# Read by `npm test` via --env-file. Names the test database and nothing else.
#
# The Postgres equivalent (db/.env.test) had to carry POSTGRES_DB, POSTGRES_USER and a password;
# a SQLite database is a path, so this is the whole file.
#
# The path is relative to the repository root, which is where npm scripts run. It is deliberately
# under data/test/ rather than beside the real database: db/sqlite/reset-test-db.mjs refuses to
# delete anything whose filename lacks "test" or that does not sit in a test directory, and
# those guards are what stop a mistyped path from destroying the evidence corpus.
REDBOT_DB=data/test/redbot-test.db
